[l_english.INVENTORY_ITEM_2UN_C02_PIANO_KEY]
Piano Keys Debris

[l_english.INVENTORY_ITEM_2UN_C02_PIANO_KEY_DESC]
Trixi collected the broken piano keys and mailed them to the address she managed to get. However, the mail was rejected and sent back — the landlord had stopped renting it out.
The landlord said that the room is now under repainting — a tenant who had just come out of prison had cut herself by the throat in the room, and the bloodstains were hard to clean. Later tenants felt it was unlucky, so the landlord had to repaint it.
At least, a reunion of father and daughter, Trixi thought, putting these broken piano keys in a box and hiding them in the darkest corner of her wagon.

[l_simp_chinese.INVENTORY_ITEM_2UN_C02_PIANO_KEY]
破碎的琴键

[l_simp_chinese.INVENTORY_ITEM_2UN_C02_PIANO_KEY_DESC]
特丽克西收集了破碎的琴键，将它们邮寄给到了她打听到的地址。然而，邮件被拒收并邮回了——房东已经停止出租了。
房东说，那间屋子正在重新刷漆——有一名刚刚从监狱里出来不久的租客在房间内割脖自杀了，血渍难以清除，后来的租客都觉得不吉利，所以不得不重新刷漆。
至少，父女团圆了吧，特丽克西这样想着，将这些破碎的琴键放在盒子内，藏在了自己的马车最黑暗的角落中。

